#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:1
msgid "_style_context"
msgstr "_style_context"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:3
msgid "Firma"
msgstr "Signature"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:9
msgid "Che problema risolve"
msgstr "What problem it solves"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:11
msgid ""
"Applica uno stile Matplotlib temporaneo e rende coerente il comportamento "
"delle figure create da `mespy`, soprattutto nei notebook IPython/Jupyter."
msgstr ""
"Applies a temporary Matplotlib style and keeps the behaviour of figures "
"created by `mespy` consistent, especially in IPython/Jupyter notebooks."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:13
msgid "Contratto sui dati in ingresso"
msgstr "Input contract"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:15
msgid ""
"`style=None` non aggiunge uno stile extra e lascia validi gli `rcParams` "
"correnti."
msgstr ""
"`style=None` does not add any extra style and leaves the current `rcParams` "
"in effect."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:16
msgid "`style=\"mespy\"` carica il file di stile incluso nel pacchetto."
msgstr "`style=\"mespy\"` loads the style file bundled with the package."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:17
msgid "Qualunque altra stringa viene passata a Matplotlib come nome stile."
msgstr "Any other string is passed to Matplotlib as a style name."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:19
msgid ""
"`histogram` passa prima lo stile da [`_resolve_style`](resolve-style.md), "
"che trasforma i nomi brevi degli stili inclusi, `\"mespy\"` compreso, nel "
"percorso del file: da `histogram` il ramo `style=\"mespy\"` riceve quindi "
"già un percorso. `lin_fit` passa invece il nome direttamente; gli stili "
"inclusi sono comunque disponibili per nome perché `import mespy` li registra"
" in Matplotlib."
msgstr ""
"`histogram` first passes the style through [`_resolve_style`](resolve-"
"style.md), which turns the short names of the bundled styles, `\"mespy\"` "
"included, into the file path: when called from `histogram`, the "
"`style=\"mespy\"` branch therefore already receives a path. `lin_fit` "
"instead passes the name directly; the bundled styles are still available by "
"name because `import mespy` registers them in Matplotlib."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:21
msgid "Dove viene usata"
msgstr "Where it is used"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:23
msgid "in [`histogram`](../../moduli/plot_utils/histogram.md)"
msgstr "in [`histogram`](../../moduli/plot_utils/histogram.md)"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:24
msgid "in [`lin_fit`](../../moduli/fit_utils/lin-fit.md)"
msgstr "in [`lin_fit`](../../moduli/fit_utils/lin-fit.md)"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:26
msgid "Come fallisce"
msgstr "How it fails"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:28
msgid ""
"Se Matplotlib non riesce a caricare lo stile richiesto, propaga l'errore del"
" sistema di stile sottostante."
msgstr ""
"If Matplotlib cannot load the requested style, it propagates the error "
"raised by the underlying style backend."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:29
msgid ""
"In ambiente notebook, alla fine del blocco mostra le nuove figure create e "
"poi le chiude per evitare la doppia visualizzazione automatica."
msgstr ""
"In notebook environments, at the end of the block it shows the new figures "
"that were created and then closes them to avoid double automatic display."

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:31
msgid "Perché resta privata"
msgstr "Why it remains private"

#: ../../source/checks/plot_utils/style-context.md:33
msgid ""
"È un dettaglio infrastrutturale condiviso dalle funzioni di visualizzazione "
"grafica. Documentarlo chiarisce il comportamento del pacchetto, ma non è "
"pensato come interfaccia pubblica stabile."
msgstr ""
"It is an infrastructural detail shared by the plotting functions. "
"Documenting it clarifies the package behaviour, but it is not intended as a "
"stable public interface."
